WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.780
This video shows how to start SWATrust and
stop it, and where it keeps its runs.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.452
The launcher is a page in the web browser
of your computer,

00:00:08.452 --> 00:00:12.690
on which you choose models, run them, look
at the results and calibrate.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.630
It runs on Windows, macOS and Linux.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.020
This tutorial is written for Linux.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.530
SWATrust needs nothing installed.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.720
The launcher, the engine and the maps are
in its folder.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.230
The chapter Download says where the
package comes from and how to unpack it.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.050
The unpacked folder holds the launcher,
the engine and the maps.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.640
SWATrust does not write into this folder.

00:00:35.141 --> 00:00:38.121
Open a terminal and go to the SWATrust
folder.

00:00:38.321 --> 00:00:39.441
Start the launcher.

00:00:39.941 --> 00:00:41.561
Read what the launcher prints.

00:00:41.761 --> 00:00:46.351
The line runs in gives the runs folder,
the one place where SWATrust writes.

00:00:46.551 --> 00:00:49.161
The line open gives the address of the
page.

00:00:49.661 --> 00:00:54.561
The part after ?t= is a key, and SWATrust
makes a new one at each start.

00:00:54.761 --> 00:00:57.608
A page opened without the key shows only a
short

00:00:57.608 --> 00:01:00.692
text that asks for the address the
launcher printed,

00:01:00.692 --> 00:01:03.301
so copy the whole address into your
browser.

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.961
Keep the terminal open while you work.

00:01:06.161 --> 00:01:08.331
The first start makes the runs folder,

00:01:08.331 --> 00:01:11.071
and the page then shows an empty list of
models.

00:01:11.572 --> 00:01:13.342
Press Ctrl-C in the terminal.

00:01:13.542 --> 00:01:15.382
Your runs stay in the runs folder.

00:01:15.882 --> 00:01:18.532
SWATrust keeps its runs in its runs
folder.

00:01:18.732 --> 00:01:22.337
To keep the runs somewhere else, such as
on a larger disk,

00:01:22.337 --> 00:01:25.072
start the launcher with --runs and a
folder.

00:01:25.572 --> 00:01:30.259
The next chapter, Quick start, downloads
one basin,

00:01:30.259 --> 00:01:34.302
02070002, North Branch Potomac, and runs
it.
